;; data/datascript-tx.edn — DataScript tx-data derived from src/association/facts.cljc
;; `association.facts/catalog` (ADR-2607141700 Wave 0). Same shape as sibling files.
;;
;; Every entry carries the verbatim span its claim rests on
;; (`:association-rule/source-quote`), the page that span was read from, and how
;; precisely that page dates the fact (`:association-rule/date-precision`).
;; scripts/verify-catalog.cljs checks both: `--live` requires the span to still
;; be in the page, and the structural pass requires the span to actually NAME
;; the date the entry claims. A citation that resolves is not the same as a
;; citation that supports, and the two look identical without the span.
;;
;; The CBI's own site (cbi.org.uk) answers HTTP 403 to this fetcher, so unlike
;; most siblings NOT ONE entry here is the organisation speaking about itself.
;; Every span is a third party: the UK public record, the UK registrar, UK
;; government departments, BusinessEurope, and en.wikipedia.org. The provenance
;; keywords say so rather than borrowing the word "official".

[#:association-rule{:id "cbi.charter-petition-1965-04-15"
                     :title "Federation of British Industries petitioned Her Majesty in Council for a new Charter under the style and title of 'The Confederation of British Industry'; the Privy Council Office notice is dated 15 April 1965 and was published in The London Gazette issue 43627, page 3777"
                     :association "cbi"
                     :isic "9411"
                     :country "GBR"
                     :kind :governance-program
                     :url "https://www.thegazette.co.uk/London/issue/43627/page/3777/data.pdf"
                     :url-provenance :uk-public-record
                     :source-article "The London Gazette, Issue 43627 (16 April 1965), Page 3777 -- Privy Council Office notice"
                     :source-quote "Notice is hereby given that a Petition of the Federation of British Industries, praying for the grant of a new Charter under the style and title of \" The Confederation of British Industry\", has been presented to Her Majesty in Council, and, Her Majesty having referred the said Petition to a Committee of the Lords of the Council, Notice is further given that all Petitions for or against such grant should be delivered to the Privy Council Office on or before the llth day of May next. 15th April 1965."
                     :established-date "1965-04-15"
                     :date-precision :day
                     :retrieved-at "2026-09-06"
